{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-05T20:47:58.374Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"77179288e1d1c04bcc4da0e8","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-998juj","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.318","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1670"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1670: pm health --full --summary silently drops --summary and emits the full projection (15.7 KB vs 636 B) with no receipt"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue #1670 (reported 2026-11-05 against 2026.11.4 from a fleet health gate run on pm-graph). Reproduced 2026-11-05 on main (e268c5b92, the 2026.11.5 cut) in a disposable one-item tracker: pm health --summary emits 636 B, while pm health --full --summary, pm health --summary --full and pm health --full each emit 15,704 B, all exit 0. Flag order does not matter and nothing in the output says the summary projection was dropped. Cause: runHealthAction in src/cli/register-operations.ts passes both summary and full to runHealth, and the full projection wins. The --full help text says it runs all checks including slow integrity, drift and vectorization, while the --strict-exit help says --full gives complete details, so one flag carries two meanings: check scope and output projection. Expected: an explicit --summary with --full runs the full check set and renders the compact summary of it (run everything, read little), which is what agents and CI gates ask for; or the combination is refused with a remedy. Never a silent drop. --strict-exit, which only implies summary, keeps its documented behaviour that --full restores complete details. Why it matters for agents: a strict gate that asks for the summary pays about 11k extra tokens per call (43.9 KB at bytes/4 on the reporter's 113-item tracker) with no omission receipt. Duplicate check: searched health summary, full, projection and flag precedence across all statuses. pm-nbht (closed) added the one-line summary mode, pm-gh1486 (closed) made passing diagnostics concise by default and pm-yjub (closed) made MCP pm_health default to the summary; none owns the precedence between --full and --summary."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","cli","gh:1670","health","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-05T20:47:58.374Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-05T20:47:58.374Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm health --full --summary runs the full check set (integrity, drift and vectorization included) and emits the summary projection, proven by a spec that compares its bytes and check names with --summary and --full on the same tracker in CLI, SDK and MCP; pm health --strict-exit --full keeps its documented complete-details output, because strict-exit only implies summary, and help text for --full and --summary states the precedence; Negative control: restoring the full projection for an explicit --summary fails the spec"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"In a fresh tracker: pm health --summary | wc -c (636), pm health --full --summary | wc -c (15704), pm health --summary --full | wc -c (15704), pm health --full | wc -c (15704); all exit 0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"An explicit --summary with --full runs every check and renders the compact summary, or the pair is refused with a remedy; never a silent drop"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"--full wins in either order and the output is byte-identical to --full alone with no warning, refusal or omission receipt"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.11.4"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"health"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1486","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-05T20:47:58.374Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-nbht","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-05T20:47:58.374Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-yjub","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-05T20:47:58.374Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"bce9db4b3c1ca6f262493238b533d699ecf58055c47141eee2f7b8107d0e0964","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2bf503cdadc40d274ab60be32212457a2411a02267b7ed7c60019d022bd770c5"}
