s so every check runs, and its complete-details projection is now only the default. resolveHealthSkipPolicy keeps an explicit summary in summaryMode with full set. selectHealthProjection picks summary, then brief, then full. runHealthAction derives the strict-exit summary only when --full is absent. The help for --summary and --full states the precedence within the ratcheted 485-token help budget, and OUTPUT_PROJECTION_CONTRACTS.md records why health composes these flags while list, graph and deps refuse them. Proven by an integration spec over the CLI, SDK client and MCP runAction on one tracker, by projection-contract and register-commands specs, and by a negative control: reverting the source fails five assertions."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Fixed: pm health --full --summary now runs every check and returns the summary projection instead of silently dropping --summary. --full stays a check-scope flag, and an explicit --summary, otherwise an explicit --brief, selects the projection. --strict-exit implies the summary only without --full. The CLI, PmClient.health and MCP action dispatch agree."}],"before_hash":"5a7ebc2d513d812797b4d8db8140f7ed686d2bf148c5c20ee59a9c86cc6c75ae","after_hash":"42059f40fddf62a5828e2f4e2964db763d59e1fe92ee10eb9c10ed4a12fccde1","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:37:26.520Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"efb869de195fd526e58db20882e227585b89b442c45b0bc25baa2cfaf367beea"}
